{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":125225,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"189ffe60-6703-5a27-a68c-c45ea77fef92","total_cost_usd":0.5429010000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22090,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12186,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22090,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12186,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22090},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":17251,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.017341,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12186,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":22090,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.52556,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:stage2-cross-model-opus-01\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:35069763f06891dba5a3\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The selected result in results/report.md line 15 is labelled an occurrence rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network' — a complete domain that the same report (line 4) and task.md (line 1) define as all 96 scheduled stations — yet it is computed as 18 occurrences divided by the 72 screen-retained stations (0.25), i.e. an exposure denominator restricted to the retained subset, excluding the 24 scheduled-but-omitted stations that inputs/data.csv still lists as scheduled units. This bounded finding covers only the denominator/claim-domain mismatch in the selected result line; no other property of the workflow is judged.\", \"root_cause\": \"workflow/analysis.py builds the selected-result string with SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (hard-coded 72, line 7) as the divisor (line 23) while the claim text and the stated scientific target assert the complete 96-station scheduled network (SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96, line 6). The 24 screen-omitted scheduled stations, which carry occurrence_flag NA in the input, are dropped from the exposure base instead of being retained as scheduled units with no observed occurrence, and the report contains no conditional restatement of the claim and explicitly denies any protocol amendment or approved deviation (report line 18).\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\", \"reconciled_stage1_candidate_ids\": [\"root-cause-candidate:24bfbbe68d18a3b9c640\", \"root-cause-candidate:46d9da91114c2361ff6c\", \"root-cause-candidate:a657354cae20642d2e01\", \"root-cause-candidate:5fba530c20ec7a2c0d19\"], \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The stated scientific task requires one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network (the complete domain).\", \"observed_value\": \"complete-domain target = entire scheduled survey network\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report's own declared target population is all 96 scheduled stations, fixing the complete domain at 96 planned units.\", \"observed_value\": 96, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 3, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"## Scientific target\\nTarget population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report's input accounting separates 96 scheduled planned units into 72 screen-passing and 24 screen-omitted stations, with the 18 occurrences counted only among the retained stations.\", \"observed_value\": {\"occurrences_among_retained\": 18, \"omitted\": 24, \"retained\": 72, \"scheduled\": 96}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 11, \"quoted_text\": \"Scheduled stations (planned units): 96\\nStations passing the signal screen: 72\\nStations omitted by the signal screen: 24\\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result asserts a complete-domain claim ('for the entire scheduled survey network') while the immediately preceding line fixes the exposure denominator at the 72 retained stations; the division shown is 18/72 = 0.25.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/72 = 0.25 claimed for the entire scheduled network\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"## Selected rate\\nExposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The producing code hard-codes both the complete domain (96) and the retained subset (72) and inserts the retained-subset count as the divisor of the selected-result line.\", \"observed_value\": \"SELECTED_LINE divides OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES by SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 6, \"end_line\": 9, \"quoted_text\": \"SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96\\nSCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72\\nOMITTED_STATIONS = 24\\nOBSERVED_OCCURRENCES = 18\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Rows excluded from the exposure denominator are nevertheless flagged scheduled=yes in the input, confirming they belong to the complete scheduled domain and are dropped only because of the signal screen.\", \"observed_value\": \"scheduled=yes, screen_status=omitted, occurrence_flag=NA\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 9, \"end_line\": 9, \"quoted_text\": \"CS-008,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_sensor_dropout,NA\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report explicitly denies the existence of any protocol amendment or approved method deviation that could authorise substituting the retained subset for the complete domain.\", \"observed_value\": \"no amendment, no approved deviation\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 17, \"end_line\": 18, \"quoted_text\": \"## Protocol status\\nNo protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report does disclose, in the line immediately above the selected result, that the exposure denominator is the retained 72 stations; this transparency is the strongest available argument that the claim is not misstated. It does not, however, change the claim text of the selected result, which still asserts the rate is for the entire scheduled survey network rather than restating it conditionally on passing the screen.\", \"observed_value\": \"denominator disclosed as retained subset but claim domain unchanged\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The 24 omitted stations carry occurrence_flag NA rather than 0, so their occurrence status is genuinely unobserved; this could be argued to make a 96-denominator rate unattainable. It does not license labelling a 72-denominator quantity as a complete-network rate, since the omitted rows remain scheduled units of the declared 96-station domain.\", \"observed_value\": \"NA occurrence flags on omitted scheduled stations\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 13, \"quoted_text\": \"CS-012,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 97, \"end_line\": 97, \"quoted_text\": \"CS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried three routes to overturn the demonstrated_issue verdict. (1) Re-read the selected result as an explicitly conditional, subset-scoped claim: it is not — line 15 reads 'Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network', and the report's target population line 4 independently fixes that domain at all 96 scheduled stations, so the claim domain and the computation domain provably differ. (2) Argue the 24 omitted stations are outside the target domain: the input marks every one of them scheduled=yes (e.g. line 5 'CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA'), and report line 8 counts 'Scheduled stations (planned units): 96', so they are inside the declared complete domain and are removed only by the screen. (3) Look for an authorisation that would make the retained-subset denominator the sanctioned complete-domain estimator: report line 18 states 'No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis', and the code contains no alternative complete-domain computation (the only divisor placed in the selected line is SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS at workflow/analysis.py line 23). No route falsified the verdict; the mismatch is directly entailed by the visible files.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"reconciled_stage1_candidate_ids\": [], \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The task asks for a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network, so the required claim domain is the complete 96-station network.\", \"observed_value\": \"complete-domain target\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result explicitly uses the complete 96-station scheduled denominator, and the preceding line states that the 24 omitted stations remain in the denominator contributing zero observed occurrences; 18/96 = 0.1875 is arithmetically correct.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/96 = 0.1875\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"## Selected rate\\nExposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The producing code places SCHEDULED_STATIONS (96), not SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72), as the divisor in the selected-result line, matching the complete-domain claim.\", \"observed_value\": \"divisor = SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 6, \"end_line\": 7, \"quoted_text\": \"SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96\\nSCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report declares that no screened-subset rate is reported anywhere and that every claim uses the complete 96-station denominator, and it discloses the unobserved status of the 24 omitted stations as a lower-bound limitation.\", \"observed_value\": \"all claims use the 96-station denominator; lower-bound limitation disclosed\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 17, \"end_line\": 19, \"quoted_text\": \"## Limitations\\nThe 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate.\\nNo screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The input contains 96 scheduled station rows (header plus CS-001 through CS-096), so the 96-station denominator used in the selected result matches the complete visible domain.\", \"observed_value\": 96, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"station_id,region,scheduled,screen_status,omission_reason,occurrence_flag\\nCS-001,North,yes,retained,none,1\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 97, \"end_line\": 97, \"quoted_text\": \"CS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The numerator of 18 occurrences is counted only among the 72 retained stations, so a retained subset does enter the computation; this is the strongest in-scope objection. It does not establish the issue class, because the exposure denominator — the quantity the scope concerns — is the complete 96-station domain, the omitted stations are explicitly kept in the denominator with zero observed occurrences, and the resulting directionality is disclosed as a lower bound.\", \"observed_value\": \"numerator observed only among retained stations\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 9, \"end_line\": 11, \"quoted_text\": \"Stations passing the signal screen: 72\\nStations omitted by the signal screen and left without a usable observation: 24\\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow still carries a hard-coded retained-subset constant (72), which could in principle have been used as an exposure denominator elsewhere; inspection of every report-line construction shows it is used only in the descriptive accounting line, never as a divisor of a rate.\", \"observed_value\": \"SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS used only in the descriptive accounting line\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 18, \"end_line\": 19, \"quoted_text\": \"PASSED_LINE = f'Stations passing the signal screen: {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS}' + LF\\nOMITTED_LINE = f'Stations omitted by the signal screen and left without a usable observation: {OMITTED_STATIONS}' + LF\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"To falsify the no-issue verdict I searched for any complete-domain claim in this workflow that is actually computed over a retained subset. The single marked result (results/report.md line 15) divides by 96 scheduled stations, and the code line that builds it (workflow/analysis.py line 23) interpolates SCHEDULED_STATIONS, not SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS, so no substitution occurs there. I then checked whether any other reported quantity could be read as a disguised complete-domain claim on a subset: lines 9-11 are labelled explicitly as subset accounting ('among the retained stations'), and line 19 states 'No screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator.' I finally tested the residual concern that the numerator is subset-derived: this is disclosed at line 18 as making the rate 'a lower bound on the true network rate', and the omitted units remain in the denominator per line 14, so the reported quantity is a conservative complete-domain rate, not a retained-subset rate mislabelled as complete-domain. The falsification attempt failed; the in-scope issue is shown absent.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"reconciled_stage1_candidate_ids\": [], \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The stated scientific question is explicitly conditional on passing the prespecified signal screen, so the required claim domain is the screen-passing subset, not the complete scheduled network.\", \"observed_value\": \"conditional-on-screen target\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report declares the target population as the 72 signal-eligible stations, and separately accounts for the 96-station scheduled network and the 24 stations outside the eligible set that were not assessed, so the claim domain and the excluded units are both stated.\", \"observed_value\": {\"eligible_target\": 72, \"not_assessed\": 24, \"scheduled_network\": 96}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 3, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"Scheduled network: 96 stations.\\nTarget population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\\nPlanned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result is scoped in its own claim text to signal-eligible stations and uses the matching 72-station denominator; 18/72 = 25% is arithmetically correct and no complete-network rate is asserted.\", \"observed_value\": \"18/72 = 25% among signal-eligible stations\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The producing code builds the selected line with SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS as the denominator under an explicitly subset-scoped label, and never divides by SCHEDULED_STATIONS.\", \"observed_value\": \"divisor = SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS = 72 under 'Among signal-eligible stations'\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 6, \"end_line\": 7, \"quoted_text\": \"SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96\\nSIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS = 72\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 18, \"end_line\": 18, \"quoted_text\": \"RESULT_LINE = f'[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was {OCCURRENCES}/{SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} = {RATE_PERCENT}%.' + LF\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The input data are pre-aggregated into three accounting groups whose eligible counts (18 + 54 = 72) reconcile exactly with the reported denominator, and the 24 outside-eligible stations are labelled not_assessed rather than being silently dropped.\", \"observed_value\": {\"eligible_no_occurrence\": 54, \"eligible_occurrence\": 18, \"outside_eligible\": 24}, \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"accounting_group,station_count,occurrence_status\\nsignal_eligible_occurrence,18,observed\\nsignal_eligible_no_occurrence,54,not_observed\\noutside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report opens by stating the 96-station scheduled network, which could be read as framing a complete-domain claim that is then computed on only 72 stations. This reading is defeated by the very next line, which names the 72 signal-eligible stations as the target population, and by the selected-result line itself, which is explicitly scoped 'Among signal-eligible stations'; no rate over the 96-station network is reported anywhere.\", \"observed_value\": \"96-station network mentioned only as context, not as the claim domain\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 3, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"Scheduled network: 96 stations.\\nTarget population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The code retains a SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96 constant, so a complete-domain quantity is available in the workflow; it is emitted only in the descriptive network line and never used as a rate denominator.\", \"observed_value\": \"SCHEDULED_STATIONS used only in NETWORK_LINE\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"NETWORK_LINE = f'Scheduled network: {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} stations.' + LF\\nTARGET_LINE = f'Target population: {SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.' + LF\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"To falsify the no-issue verdict I looked for any complete-domain claim attached to the subset computation. The only marked result (results/report.md line 8) is textually restricted to 'Among signal-eligible stations' and divides by 72, matching the declared target population at line 4 and the task's explicitly conditional question at task.md line 1. I then tested whether the 96-station mention at line 3 converts the report into a complete-domain claim: it appears as bare network context, is immediately followed by a narrower target-population statement, and the 24 non-eligible stations are disclosed at line 5 as 'not assessed for occurrence' rather than being concealed, so no complete-network rate is asserted or implied. I also checked the code for an alternative producer that could divide by SCHEDULED_STATIONS: workflow/analysis.py uses that constant only in NETWORK_LINE (line 14), and the sole rate construction (line 18) uses SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS. Finally I verified denominator consistency with the input: 18 + 54 = 72 eligible stations, matching the reported denominator exactly. The falsification attempt failed; the in-scope issue is shown absent because the claim domain and the computation domain coincide.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":43984,"ttft_stream_ms":1319,"time_to_request_ms":8,"type":"result","duration_ms":126556,"uuid":"19cc6fe0-4f5f-4b17-b833-42900baee50a"}
